XNU en0 ifnet in poll mode over the reviewed Wi-Fi data path (P-W3, T-4d29; SPEC-WIFI Part E EN0 block, rows EN1-EN12).

Cause: patch 0073's ue0 ifnet is a USB ECM pattern: LEGACY without NX_NOAUTO, RX without the 2-byte pad, no BPF attach or taps, no link event, a silent
EOPNOTSUPP in ioctl, and a static address hard-coded in the patch (rule 4, rule 8). Wi-Fi needs the same ifnet with the E-1..E-7 rules of SPEC-WIFI.
Fix: new bsd/dev/sweet_wlan_en0.h (the logic: ifnet_allocate_extended with IFNET_INIT_LEGACY|IFNET_INIT_NX_NOAUTO, attach, lladdr after attach from the caller,
bpf_attach + taps, RX mbuf chain with pad and per-buffer lengths, pkt_hdr handoff, TX output -> swdp_build_txpost + swdp_plan_tx + swdp_audit, a poll function
that reads the D2H write index and reposts rx buffers, no interrupt registration, link events through ifnet_event, SIOCGIFMEDIA, ioctl GAP lines, the static
address only from boot-arg pixos_en0_ip), the two data-path headers it uses (verbatim copies of shim/sweet_wlan_data.h and sweet_wlan_data_plan.h, the
reviewed layouts of T-71e2, with the one <stdio.h> line swapped for <sys/systm.h>), and bsd/dev/sweet_wlan_en0.c (glue: KPI headers, if_xflags, the SIOCAIFADDR
socket, the unwired DP15 bus whose exec() refuses). Generated by tools/gen-wlan-en0-patch from shim/; shim/build.sh refuses a stale copy.
Tests: shim/wlan_en0_host_test.c (stub ifnet/mbuf/bpf, fake bus) with one mutant per rule in tools/test_wlan_en0_mutants.py. Not compiled against XNU here
(CI builds the tree), not run on hardware; nothing calls sweet_wlan_en0_init() yet (T-4505 wires it). The msgbuf transport (DP15) is not wired.

